Description: Google Pixel Buds support (battery, noise control, multipoint)
 kbuds talks to Google Pixel Buds Pro, Pro 2 and 2a over their Maestro
 Bluetooth channel. It contains:
  - kbudsd, a per-user daemon (systemd user service) that owns the channel,
    exposes the buds on D-Bus and publishes their battery to BlueZ/UPower;
  - kbudsctl, a command-line client;
  - kbuds, a Qt Quick settings application;
  - a WirePlumber rule that suspends the buds' A2DP sink after 1 s, so that
    a multipoint phone can take the audio back quickly.
